      "message": "PTAL, thanks!\n\nThe SPIR-V backend is the easiest one. Other backends are far more difficult. For example, to translate `array\u003cf32, 8\u003e clipDistances [[clip_distances]]`:\n1. On HLSL, the output should be:\n   ```\n   float4 clipDistances0 : SV_ClipDistance0;\n   float4 clipDistances1 : SV_ClipDistance1;\n   ```\n2. On MSL, the output should be a C-style array:\n   ```\n   float clipDistances[8] [[ clip_distance]];\n   ```\n  `tint_array\u003cfloat, 1\u003e clipDistance [[clip_distance]]` is not allowed.\n3. On GLSL (ES), the tint end2end test will fail because glslang doesn\u0027t support `GL_EXT_clip_cull_distance` (https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glslang/issues/566)\n\nMaybe I need your help on the above issues 😊",
